content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "The reported drive-end bearing-housing vibration of 5.5 mm/s RMS is within Figure 3 Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS): “Restricted — plan maintenance.” It is below the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/Zone D boundary, so this reading alone does not trigger the site rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone. The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified, so the overall classification remains subject to obtaining the non-drive-end reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Last month's 3.0 mm/s RMS reading was in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, “Long-term operation”). The reported increase is 2.5 mm/s RMS and represents a change from Zone B to Zone C, supporting planned investigation rather than continued routine monitoring only.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drive-end housing temperature of 76°C exceeds the normal limit of 70°C by 6°C, but is below the 80°C alarm and 90°C trip values. Bearing temperatures are specified on the housing surface. Because 76°C is not above the manufacturer's 80°C alarm limit, the SSP-07 requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not currently triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 is selected to implement the Zone C instruction to plan maintenance, rather than P1: neither the current vibration reading nor the current temperature meets the documented immediate-stop or mandatory-P1 condition. No immediate stop is therefore directed on the reported readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The troubleshooting table associates shaft-seal leakage with mechanical-seal replacement, whereas the applicable reported symptoms are high vibration and elevated bearing temperature. Seal replacement is therefore not included in the base scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear and/or misalignment are the leading documented possibilities to investigate because both appear as causes of high vibration and high bearing temperature; the evidence does not distinguish between them.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature. Check grease quantity before attributing the temperature rise solely to bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation are additional documented causes of high vibration. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH to retain or eliminate these possibilities.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before dismantling, measure and record vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Record the drive-end housing surface temperature and repeat the comparison with the 70°C normal, 80°C alarm and 90°C trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any vibration reading falls in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature rises above 80°C, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, capture the operating and suction conditions needed to check NPSH and investigate cavitation. Do not assume a bearing defect before completing the documented alignment, bearing, impeller and NPSH checks.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal inspection, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "When back pull-out access is required, use the back pull-out arrangement to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg; use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment specified in the safety controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check grease quantity, inspect both bearings and the impeller, assess misalignment, and review the NPSH findings. Record the inspection results so that bearing wear, over-greasing, misalignment, impeller imbalance/damage and cavitation can be differentiated.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair. For listed fasteners actually disturbed, reassemble using Table 5 values on lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm if removed; and M16 casing bolts 210 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Accept only parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On completion, record vibration on both bearing housings as the post-work comparison and resume the weekly route. Continue to classify the highest housing reading and apply the Zone D stop/notification and above-alarm temperature escalation rules.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "NOT SPECIFIED IN EVIDENCE — BEARING PAIR",
      "description": "One bearing pair comprising both pump bearings, conditional on inspection confirming the manual's replacement criterion. Both bearings must be replaced together; exact drive-end and non-drive-end part numbers must be confirmed before issue.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to this site pump. For work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Removal of the 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 5.5 mm/s RMS reading is not in the highest severity zone. If subsequent measurement places the highest housing reading in Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are not added on the supplied dosing evidence: that evidence identifies chemically dosed pumps P-101 through P-106, while this asset is P-107. Reassess and apply those controls if the line duty is found to differ from the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-pair replacement is confirmed and executed, the standard allowance is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the work moves the motor or bearing housing, allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician for the required laser alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual's Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts, whereas service bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, specifies 30 Nm for cartridge seal HF3-450B and supersedes seal HF3-450. P-107's serial HF3-22950 is within the bulletin range of HF3-22000 and above. Therefore, if seal replacement is separately authorised on this asset, use HF3-450B at 30 Nm, not HF3-450 at 25 Nm. The bulletin does not change the other Table 5 torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any authorised installation of HF3-450B, its pre-set design means no seal-setting sleeve measurement is needed. This does not eliminate the manual's sleeve condition inspection when the seal and sleeve are withdrawn: replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. No seal replacement is presently included in the base scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration velocity? C06 requires weekly measurement of both housings and classification of the highest reading; only the drive-end value is reported.",
    "What are the exact bearing part numbers and the bearing/impeller acceptance or wear limits? C09 and C10 specify inspection and the bearing-pair rule but do not provide those part numbers or detailed acceptance criteria.",
    "What grease type and correct grease quantity apply? C09 directs the technician to check grease quantity, but the evidence provides neither a specification nor a numerical fill limit.",
    "What are the suction conditions, NPSH available and the HF-300 NPSH requirement needed to complete the cavitation check directed by C09?",
    "What operating restriction and completion date apply while the pump remains in Zone C, and does site planning confirm the selected P2 priority? C07 says “Restricted — plan maintenance” without a time limit, while C15 defines the highest-zone stop rule and the above-alarm P1 rule but no P2/P3 convention.",
    "What labour allowance should be used for diagnosis, NPSH/grease checks, back pull-out inspection and general reassembly? C12 tabulates only mechanical-seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment.",
    "If seal replacement is later authorised, what is the required new casing gasket's part number? C10 requires a new casing gasket but does not identify it."
  ]
}
